From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qbtOS Developers <qbtos@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 22:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] initcall: trace pre-console calls on debug UART

Raspberry Pi development images need actionable output when an early U-Boot
initcall stalls before driver-model serial is available. Print the initcall
name and its successful return while the normal console is unavailable.

The debug UART helpers compile to no-ops when CONFIG_DEBUG_UART is disabled.
Once the normal console is active, avoid the debug UART so it cannot conflict
with driver-model serial.

Upstream: Not applicable; qbtOS development-only early-boot instrumentation
Signed-off-by: qbtOS Developers <qbtos@example.invalid>
---
 include/initcall.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/initcall.h b/include/initcall.h
index b64854feef..678db2fa33 100644
--- a/include/initcall.h
+++ b/include/initcall.h
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #ifndef __INITCALL_H
 #define __INITCALL_H
 
+#include <debug_uart.h>
 #include <asm/types.h>
 #include <event.h>
 #include <hang.h>
@@ -14,11 +15,15 @@ _Static_assert(EVT_COUNT < 256, "Can only support 256 event types with 8 bits");
 
 #define INITCALL(_call) \
 	do { \
+		if (!(gd->flags & GD_FLG_HAVE_CONSOLE)) \
+			printascii("[init] " #_call "\n"); \
 		if (_call()) { \
 			printf("%s(): initcall %s() failed\n", __func__, \
 			       #_call); \
 			hang(); \
 		} \
+		if (!(gd->flags & GD_FLG_HAVE_CONSOLE)) \
+			printascii("[ ok ] " #_call "\n"); \
 	} while (0)
 
 #define INITCALL_EVT(_evt) \
-- 
